---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About">
	<h1>About</h1>

	<p>
		I'm an ML engineer at DataNimbus in Plano, TX. Most of my work is taking messy,
		real-world data and turning it into models that actually run in production, which
		usually means the modeling is the easy half and everything around it is the
		interesting half.
	</p>

	<p>
		Recent work: demand forecasting for home services companies, churn and lifetime
		value models, an agentic financial intelligence platform, and migrating a legacy
		Java ML pipeline to Python on Databricks for a marketing data company. I've also
		been building an internal platform for ML experimentation and model management on
		Databricks Apps, which I wrote about in <a href="/blog/pushing-the-limits-of-databricks-apps/">Pushing the Limits of Databricks Apps</a>.
	</p>

	<p>
		Before DataNimbus I was at Persistent Systems and Capiot Software, working mostly on
		health data (ECG signal processing) and address and entity matching at scale. I did
		my MS in Computer Engineering at NYU Tandon.
	</p>

	<h2>Outside of work</h2>
	<p>
		I shoot film. The latest frames end up on <a href="https://instagram.com/upafilm">@upafilm</a>.
	</p>
	<div class="ig">
		<!-- Shown until the embed reports it rendered; stays up where it's blocked
		     (e.g. Firefox tracking protection) or JS is off. -->
		<a class="ig-fallback" href="https://instagram.com/upafilm">
			<span class="ig-handle">@upafilm</span>
			<span class="ig-cta">See the photos on Instagram &rarr;</span>
		</a>
		<iframe
			class="ig-embed"
			src="https://www.instagram.com/upafilm/embed/"
			title="@upafilm on Instagram"
		></iframe>
	</div>

	<h2>Right now</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Building an ML experimentation platform on Databricks Apps</li>
		<li>Open to new roles. <a href="/contact/">Say hi</a>.</li>
	</ul>
</Layout>

<script>
	// Instagram's embed posts MEASURE messages with its rendered height. Only once one
	// arrives do we reveal the iframe and hide the fallback.
	const wrap = document.querySelector('.ig');
	const frame = wrap?.querySelector('iframe');
	window.addEventListener('message', (e) => {
		if (!frame || e.origin !== 'https://www.instagram.com' || e.source !== frame.contentWindow) return;
		let msg;
		try {
			msg = typeof e.data === 'string' ? JSON.parse(e.data) : e.data;
		} catch {
			return;
		}
		const height = msg?.type === 'MEASURE' ? Number(msg.details?.height) : 0;
		if (height > 0) {
			frame.style.height = `${height}px`;
			wrap.classList.add('loaded');
		}
	});
</script>

<style>
	.ig {
		max-width: 540px;
		margin: 1rem 0;
	}

	.ig-embed {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: 0;
		border: none;
	}

	.ig.loaded .ig-embed {
		border-radius: 4px;
	}

	.ig.loaded .ig-fallback {
		display: none;
	}

	.ig-fallback {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.25rem;
		padding: 1.25rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: 4px;
		background: var(--bg-raised);
	}

	.ig-fallback:hover {
		border-color: var(--accent-dim);
	}

	.ig-handle {
		color: var(--text);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.ig-cta {
		color: var(--accent);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
</style>
